<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovnaft consolidated H1 net drops.</title>
<headline>Slovnaft consolidated H1 net drops.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited consolidated results for six months to June 30, 1996, according to international accounting standards: (in SKK millions)</p>
<p> After-tax result	 113 profit  vs    835 profit</p>
<p> Pre-tax result	   322 profit  vs  1,712 profit</p>
<p> Operating result	 703 profit  vs  1,709 profit</p>
<p> Revenue from sales   16,498	   vs 18,914</p>
<p> Costs of sales	 13,444	   vs 14,432</p>
<p> Write-offs		  614	   vs    509</p>
<p> Financial revenue	  55	   vs     19</p>
<p> Other operating costs   489	   vs  1,017</p>
<p> Fixed assets	   22,852	   vs 20,565</p>
<p> Current assets	 15,758	   vs 11,215</p>
<p> Basic capital	  16,469	   vs 13,169</p>
<p> Own capital	    21,827	   vs 18,926</p>
<p> Long-term liabilities 2,922	   vs  1,204</p>
<p> Short-term liabil.   12,192	   vs 10,299</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Slovnaft a.s.. It is Slovakia's sole crude oil refiner and controls roughly 80 percent of the domestic petrol station market. The company shut 70 percent of its refining capacity from early March to end- April to complete required major maintenence.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
